    "reason": "The evidence clearly gives the subject and the change: the deprecated `store.max-look-back-period` CLI flag and its YAML settings are removed, and `querier.max-query-lookback` replaces them [ev-dc20110f4f4b][ev-f7fa153951ef][ev-b4e42b3143e3]. The open aspect is consequence, and nothing in the evidence says what happens to an environment that still sets the flag or the YAML key. The release note, the upgrade-guide section and the PR description and file list don't say whether Loki rejects the config and fails to start, or ignores the setting and silently drops the lookback limit [ev-9d46fd4b4f32][ev-f964812ad69c]. To decide the consequence kind we need the PR diff (pkg/storage/config/store.go, pkg/loki/loki.go) or documentation that states how Loki handles the removed flag or YAML field.",
